      answerHtml: `<p><strong>Gibsonton spent most of the twentieth century as the winter quarters for traveling carnival and circus workers</strong>, which is where the nickname Gibtown comes from. The International Independent Showmen Association is still based here, and its 55,000-square-foot museum sits just up Riverview Drive.</p><p>The real-estate consequence is practical rather than sentimental: that history left pockets of <strong>unusually permissive legacy zoning</strong>, which is why you will find parcels with large outbuildings, equipment storage and commercial-adjacent uses sitting next to ordinary houses. Before you buy, check the zoning and permitted uses on your parcel <em>and on the parcels around you</em> what a neighbor is allowed to do matters as much here as what you are allowed to do.</p>`,
