      answerHtml: `<p><strong>Pick Riverview if you want resale liquidity and amenities; pick Gibsonton if you want the lowest entry price with the same interstate access.</strong></p><p><strong>Riverview</strong> is the much larger, much more heavily built-out market, which means a deeper buyer pool when you sell, more new construction to choose from, and more master-planned communities with pools and trails.</p><p>Gibsonton's 156 closed sales in the twelve months ending October 2026 is a fraction of Riverview's volume, which cuts both ways, fewer competing listings when you sell, but thinner comps and a smaller buyer pool. The two are close enough geographically that your real decision is <strong>amenities and liquidity versus price</strong>.</p>`,
