      answerHtml: `<p><strong>Five items, in this order:</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Zoning and permitted uses</strong> on your parcel and the adjacent ones, the legacy mixed-use pattern here is not what you would expect from a subdivision.</li><li><strong>County water and sewer vs private well and septic</strong>, which varies address to address.</li><li><strong>A FEMA flood determination.</strong> Gibsonton fronts Tampa Bay at East Bay and has tidal creeks running inland, so exposure changes sharply over short distances.</li><li><strong>The Hillsborough County hurricane evacuation zone</strong>, a separate designation from the flood zone.</li><li><strong>Genuinely comparable sales</strong>, because a thin market invites bad pricing in both directions.</li></ul><p>None of these show up in listing photos, and all five can change what the property is worth to you. Call (813) 733-7907 to walk through a specific parcel.</p>`,
